'' RUN: 'func ((5 - 1) + 1) * 0' is one call whose argument is the whole expression. The
'' paren group was taken as the call's argument list and '* 0' dropped: fbc prints 0, 5, 6,
'' tiko printed 5, 5, 2. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/paren-call-operand.bas -o tests/codegen/parencalloperand.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/parencalloperand.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: n= 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: n= 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: n= 6
